kind=DOCSTRING_MODULE	text="""""""Closes the remaining Gate-3 node-type gap that isn't `match`: assert, break/continue, elif chains, implicit string concatenation, f-string interpolation forms (literal `{{`/`}}` escapes, a nested dynamic format spec, and a plain format spec), backslash line continuation, `not`, a plain set display, slice forms, and a typed parameter with a default value. Each construct was confirmed against `ast.parse` before staging; none of this is exotic, it is simply syntax the mined corpus's six projects happened not to phrase this way often enough to be sampled. """""""	startLine=1	startColumn=0	endLine=9	endColumn=3	ownerHash=PY_METHOD_6fa4ea82d6c14c10951458a04c0851cd	commentIndex=0	ownerKind=MODULE	pyModuleLinkHash=PY_MODULE_99797da9f6b8580a03c8a2f7bf6898ea	typeCommentPayload=	isDocstring=true	serviceVersionLinkHash=SERVICE_VERSION_00000000000000000000000000000000	pyCommentUniqueHash=PY_COMMENT_3f8232e0ecb3f9f186d9354cdba9c3d8
kind=DOCSTRING_MODULE	text="""""""Declaration site. Everything else in the benchmark resolves back to here."""""""	startLine=1	startColumn=0	endLine=1	endColumn=79	ownerHash=PY_METHOD_386e258a8f1c3adf61f362eca468c230	commentIndex=0	ownerKind=MODULE	pyModuleLinkHash=PY_MODULE_0af7a9df251376bafe876afe4a32f46e	typeCommentPayload=	isDocstring=true	serviceVersionLinkHash=SERVICE_VERSION_00000000000000000000000000000000	pyCommentUniqueHash=PY_COMMENT_dc7d62d0382f2b2ed66fca4138a29c10
kind=DOCSTRING_MODULE	text="""""""Private name mangling (`__name` -> `_ClassName__name`), pinned down at the boundary CPython actually draws it at, rather than the commonly mis-stated ""any double-underscore attribute"" version: - It mangles the identifier **textually**, recursively through every nested def/lambda/comprehension inside the class body, using the *nearest enclosing class* at that point in the source — not the outermost one. - It applies to bare identifiers (which show up as mangled symtable symbols — Gate-1 checkable) exactly the same way it applies to attribute-access names like `self.__x` (`ast.Attribute.attr` is left UNMANGLED by `ast.parse`; the substitution only happens later, in bytecode compilation's `co_names`). That second form is confirmed against `compile()`/`dis` below but is invisible to both `ast` and `symtable`, so it is not something Gate 1 or Gate 2 can adjudicate — flagged in the manifest, not asserted as oracle-verified. - Exactly two leading underscores and *at most one* trailing underscore qualifies. Two leading AND two-or-more trailing (a ""dunder"", e.g. `__init__`, `__x__`) is explicitly exempt. """""""	startLine=1	startColumn=0	endLine=20	endColumn=3	ownerHash=PY_METHOD_57b34b04c8f99b558638ddf8a40a1baa	commentIndex=0	ownerKind=MODULE	pyModuleLinkHash=PY_MODULE_75dd800d24b53dd3ca1d826ca1525876	typeCommentPayload=	isDocstring=true	serviceVersionLinkHash=SERVICE_VERSION_00000000000000000000000000000000	pyCommentUniqueHash=PY_COMMENT_2a8aa078372d7e8bd05fedaa81b31fc7
kind=DOCSTRING_MODULE	text="""""""SELF and SUPER, entirely in-root so the ceiling stays 100%."""""""	startLine=1	startColumn=0	endLine=1	endColumn=65	ownerHash=PY_METHOD_9285560c8f45e1e0c9ea4712a036d1ee	commentIndex=0	ownerKind=MODULE	pyModuleLinkHash=PY_MODULE_0a821397f31f9644e27278ab1de4362b	typeCommentPayload=	isDocstring=true	serviceVersionLinkHash=SERVICE_VERSION_00000000000000000000000000000000	pyCommentUniqueHash=PY_COMMENT_97ac9d54d43aa4f87a7325dd16faaf4c
kind=DOCSTRING_MODULE	text="""""""Scope-resolution edge cases that are easy for a hand-rolled resolver to get wrong even though CPython's own rule is simple and uniform: class bodies are *never* an enclosing scope for anything nested inside them (methods, comprehensions, nested classes) — only module and function scopes participate in that chain. Every case here is confirmed against `compile()`/`symtable` before being staged; several are runtime NameErrors that are nonetheless perfectly valid, parseable syntax. """""""	startLine=1	startColumn=0	endLine=8	endColumn=3	ownerHash=PY_METHOD_a86c44fd87550eb3aef8b5ebfaaeec46	commentIndex=0	ownerKind=MODULE	pyModuleLinkHash=PY_MODULE_7c5670e72548f0c21d5e8710e5a91903	typeCommentPayload=	isDocstring=true	serviceVersionLinkHash=SERVICE_VERSION_00000000000000000000000000000000	pyCommentUniqueHash=PY_COMMENT_674b321f68ba38910c2aef814d40641b
kind=DOCSTRING_MODULE	text="""""""Second match/case fixture: nesting depth, splat position variants, and guards that reference multiple pattern-bound names — deliberately different shapes from match_class_and_sequence_patterns.py rather than repeats. """""""	startLine=1	startColumn=0	endLine=4	endColumn=3	ownerHash=PY_METHOD_c7fadbc953cbe6b4c4dbbd8e698d809a	commentIndex=0	ownerKind=MODULE	pyModuleLinkHash=PY_MODULE_fcb43aba22913355ac115ae9c4556240	typeCommentPayload=	isDocstring=true	serviceVersionLinkHash=SERVICE_VERSION_00000000000000000000000000000000	pyCommentUniqueHash=PY_COMMENT_45e71066ad207593fc398080dd579ebc
